<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Valka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valga (Latvian: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valka">Valka</a>, German: Walk) is a town on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and Latvia, divided between the two countries since 1920. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a frequent meeting place of the Livonian Landtag, the diet of the Livonian Confederation, whose founding agreement was made there in 1435. Its Estonian half is Valga and its Latvian half Valka.</p></div>
